/*
program -02
----------------
 Calculator Program with Various Methods
Create a Calculator class with the following specifications:

Attributes:

result (double): Holds the latest calculation result.

Methods:

void add(double num): Adds num to result and updates it.
void subtract(double num): Subtracts num from result and updates it.
void multiply(double num): Multiplies result by num and updates it.
void divide(double num): Divides result by num and updates it, ensuring there’s no division by zero.
double getResult(): Returns the current result.

Task:

Create a main method to:

Instantiate the Calculator class.
Perform a sequence of operations (e.g., addition, subtraction, multiplication, division) using method calls.Print the result after each operation.
*/
class PtwoElc 
{
	public static void main(String[] args) 
	{
		PtwoBlc obj1 =new PtwoBlc();
		System.out.println(obj1.getResult());
		obj1.add(10);
		System.out.println(obj1.getResult());
		obj1.subtract(10);
		System.out.println(obj1.getResult());
		obj1.multiply(10);
		System.out.println(obj1.getResult());
		obj1.division(10);
		System.out.println(obj1.getResult());
		
		
	}
}
